  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study relies on primary data from transport providers to model these impacts, which may introduce self-reporting biases regarding transit times and cost indicators.",
      "what": "This study analyzes the combined impact of India's National Logistics Policy (2022) and artificial intelligence adoption on logistics performance and cost reduction. Using primary data from 500 transport providers, the empirical model incorporates geographical information, freight volumes, vehicle turnaround times, and cost indicators across major transport corridors. The findings demonstrate a 30.5% reduction in average transit time following the policy's implementation.",
      "why": "It quantifies the joint impact of national policy frameworks and digital technology adoption on logistics efficiency, providing empirical evidence of transit time reductions that can guide future infrastructure investments and digital connectivity strategies in India."
